IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-amendment.l4 -- sections 601 to 605 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: amendment of indictments; inspection and copies of documents; release of exhibits for testing). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Section 601 -- Amending defective indictment or count`

-- (1), first sentence: an objection for a defect apparent on the face is taken by motion to quash before the plea and, after the plea, only by leave of the court.
-- src:12747 | 601 (1) An objection to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face, shall be taken by motion to quash the indictment or count before the accused enters a plea, and, after the accused has entered a plea, only by leave of the court before which the proceedings take place. The court before which an objection is taken under this section may, if it considers it necessary, order the indictment or count to be amended to cure the defect.
@ref s 601(1) (src:12747-12747)
GIVEN `the objection is to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is taken by motion to quash the indictment or count` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has entered a plea` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court before which the proceedings take place has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(1) the objection may be taken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the objection is to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An objection to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face"
        IF `the accused has entered a plea` THEN
            (IF `the court before which the proceedings take place has given leave` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the accused has entered a plea, only by leave of the court before which the proceedings take place" [M-a]
        IF `the objection is taken by motion to quash the indictment or count` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be taken by motion to quash the indictment or count before the accused enters a plea" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- (1), second sentence: the court before which an objection is taken may, if it considers it necessary, order the indictment or count amended to cure the defect.
-- src:12747 | 601 (1) An objection to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face, shall be taken by motion to quash the indictment or count before the accused enters a plea, and, after the accused has entered a plea, only by leave of the court before which the proceedings take place. The court before which an objection is taken under this section may, if it considers it necessary, order the indictment or count to be amended to cure the defect.
@ref s 601(1) (src:12747-12747)
GIVEN `an objection is taken under section 601` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(1) the court may order the indictment or count to be amended to cure the defect` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an objection is taken under section 601` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court before which an objection is taken under this section"
        IF NOT `the court considers it necessary` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if it considers it necessary, order the indictment or count to be amended" [F:may-if]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12749 | (2) Subject to this section, a court may, on the trial of an indictment, amend the indictment or a count therein or a particular that is furnished under section 587, to make the indictment, count or particular conform to the evidence, where there is a variance between the evidence and
-- src:12750 | (a) a count in the indictment as preferred; or
-- src:12751 | (b) a count in the indictment
-- src:12752 | (i) as amended, or
-- src:12753 | (ii) as it would have been if it had been amended in conformity with any particular that has been furnished pursuant to section 587.
@ref s 601(2) (src:12749-12753)
GIVEN `the trial is a trial of an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a variance between the evidence and a count in the indictment as preferred, as amended, or as it would have been if amended in conformity with a particular furnished under section 587` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(2) the court may amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` MEANS
    IF `the trial is a trial of an indictment` AND `there is a variance between the evidence and a count in the indictment as preferred, as amended, or as it would have been if amended in conformity with a particular furnished under section 587`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a court may, on the trial of an indictment, amend the indictment or a count therein or a particular that is furnished under section 587, to make the indictment, count or particular conform to the evidence, where there is a variance" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:12755 | (3) Subject to this section, a court shall, at any stage of the proceedings, amend the indictment or a count therein as may be necessary where it appears
-- src:12756 | (a) that the indictment has been preferred under a particular Act of Parliament instead of another Act of Parliament;
-- src:12757 | (b) that the indictment or a count thereof
-- src:12758 | (i) fails to state or states defectively anything that is requisite to constitute the offence,
-- src:12759 | (ii) does not negative an exception that should be negatived,
-- src:12760 | (iii) is in any way defective in substance,
-- src:12761 | and the matters to be alleged in the proposed amendment are disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry or on the trial; or
-- src:12762 | (c) that the indictment or a count thereof is in any way defective in form.
@ref s 601(3) (src:12755-12762)
DECLARE `s 601(3) the defect` IS ONE OF
    `s 601(3)(a) the indictment has been preferred under a particular Act of Parliament instead of another Act of Parliament`
    `s 601(3)(b) the indictment or a count fails to state or states defectively anything requisite to constitute the offence, does not negative an exception that should be negatived, or is in any way defective in substance`
    `s 601(3)(c) the indictment or a count is in any way defective in form`
    `s 601(3) none of those`

-- src:12755 | (3) Subject to this section, a court shall, at any stage of the proceedings, amend the indictment or a count therein as may be necessary where it appears
-- src:12756 | (a) that the indictment has been preferred under a particular Act of Parliament instead of another Act of Parliament;
-- src:12757 | (b) that the indictment or a count thereof
-- src:12758 | (i) fails to state or states defectively anything that is requisite to constitute the offence,
-- src:12759 | (ii) does not negative an exception that should be negatived,
-- src:12760 | (iii) is in any way defective in substance,
-- src:12761 | and the matters to be alleged in the proposed amendment are disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry or on the trial; or
-- src:12762 | (c) that the indictment or a count thereof is in any way defective in form.
@ref s 601(3) (src:12755-12762)
GIVEN defect IS A `s 601(3) the defect`
      `the matters to be alleged in the proposed amendment are disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry or on the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(3) the court must amend the indictment or count as may be necessary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF defect EQUALS `s 601(3) none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a court shall, at any stage of the proceedings, amend the indictment or a count therein as may be necessary where it appears" (none of (a) to (c) appears) [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF defect EQUALS `s 601(3)(b) the indictment or a count fails to state or states defectively anything requisite to constitute the offence, does not negative an exception that should be negatived, or is in any way defective in substance` AND (NOT `the matters to be alleged in the proposed amendment are disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry or on the trial`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the matters to be alleged in the proposed amendment are disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry or on the trial" [M-a] [F:duty]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12764 | (4) The court shall, in considering whether or not an amendment should be made to the indictment or a count in it, consider
-- src:12765 | (a) the matters disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry;
-- src:12766 | (b) the evidence taken on the trial, if any;
-- src:12767 | (c) the circumstances of the case;
-- src:12768 | (d) whether the accused has been misled or prejudiced in his defence by any variance, error or omission mentioned in subsection (2) or (3); and
-- src:12769 | (e) whether, having regard to the merits of the case, the proposed amendment can be made without injustice being done.
@ref s 601(4) (src:12764-12769)
GIVEN `the court has considered the matters disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence taken on the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has considered the evidence taken on the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has considered the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has considered whether the accused has been misled or prejudiced in their defence by any variance, error or omission mentioned in subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has considered whether, having regard to the merits of the case, the proposed amendment can be made without injustice being done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(4) the court has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether an amendment should be made` MEANS
    IF     `the court has considered the matters disclosed by the evidence taken on the preliminary inquiry`
       AND (`the court has considered the evidence taken on the trial` OR (NOT `there is evidence taken on the trial`))
       AND `the court has considered the circumstances of the case`
       AND `the court has considered whether the accused has been misled or prejudiced in their defence by any variance, error or omission mentioned in subsection (2) or (3)`
       AND `the court has considered whether, having regard to the merits of the case, the proposed amendment can be made without injustice being done`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall, in considering whether or not an amendment should be made to the indictment or a count in it, consider" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12771 | (4.1) A variance between the indictment or a count therein and the evidence taken is not material with respect to
-- src:12772 | (a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, if it is proved that the indictment was preferred within the prescribed period of limitation, if any; or
-- src:12773 | (b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen, if it is proved that it arose within the territorial jurisdiction of the court.
@ref s 601(4.1) (src:12771-12773)
DECLARE `s 601(4.1) the variance is with respect to` IS ONE OF
    `s 601(4.1)(a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 601(4.1)(b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen`
    `s 601(4.1) something else`

-- src:12771 | (4.1) A variance between the indictment or a count therein and the evidence taken is not material with respect to
-- src:12772 | (a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, if it is proved that the indictment was preferred within the prescribed period of limitation, if any; or
-- src:12773 | (b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen, if it is proved that it arose within the territorial jurisdiction of the court.
@ref s 601(4.1) (src:12771-12773)
GIVEN respect IS A `s 601(4.1) the variance is with respect to`
      `it is proved that the indictment was preferred within the prescribed period of limitation, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the subject-matter arose within the territorial jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 601(4.1) the variance is material` MEANS
    CONSIDER respect
    WHEN `s 601(4.1)(a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN
        (IF `it is proved that the indictment was preferred within the prescribed period of limitation, if any`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A variance between the indictment or a count therein and the evidence taken is not material with respect to (a) the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed, if it is proved that the indictment was preferred within the prescribed period of limitation" [M-a]
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is proved that the indictment was preferred within the prescribed period of limitation, if any" (not proved: the subsection does not say the variance is material)
    WHEN `s 601(4.1)(b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen` THEN
        (IF `it is proved that the subject-matter arose within the territorial jurisdiction of the court`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the place where the subject-matter of the proceedings is alleged to have arisen, if it is proved that it arose within the territorial jurisdiction of the court" [M-a]
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is proved that it arose within the territorial jurisdiction of the court" (not proved: the subsection does not say the variance is material)
    WHEN `s 601(4.1) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of time and place only

