§ `Section 603 -- Right of accused`

-- (a), (b): the accused is entitled, after being ordered to stand trial or at the trial, to inspect without charge, and to receive a copy on payment of a reasonable fee fixed under the Attorney General's tariff.
-- src:12792 | 603 An accused is entitled, after he has been ordered to stand trial or at his trial,
-- src:12793 | (a) to inspect without charge the indictment, his own statement, the evidence and the exhibits, if any; and
-- src:12794 | (b) to receive, on payment of a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province, a copy
-- src:12795 | (i) of the evidence,
-- src:12796 | (ii) of his own statement, if any, and
-- src:12797 | (iii) of the indictment;
-- src:12798 | but the trial shall not be postponed to enable the accused to secure copies unless the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure them before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on the part of the accused.
@ref s 603 (src:12792-12798)
DECLARE `s 603(a) what the accused inspects` IS ONE OF
    `s 603(a) the indictment`
    `s 603(a) the accused’s own statement`
    `s 603(a) the evidence`
    `s 603(a) the exhibits, if any`
    `s 603(a) something else`

