        IF NOT `the accused has been ordered to stand trial or is at their trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An accused is entitled, after he has been ordered to stand trial or at his trial" [F:entitled] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the accused pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to receive, on payment of a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province" [F:entitled] [M-a]
        IF thing EQUALS `s 603(b) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "a copy (i) of the evidence, (ii) of his own statement, if any, and (iii) of the indictment"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The proviso, as a BAR: the trial shall not be postponed to enable the accused to secure copies unless the court is satisfied that the failure was not attributable to the accused's lack of diligence.
-- src:12798 | but the trial shall not be postponed to enable the accused to secure copies unless the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure them before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on the part of the accused.
@ref s 603 (src:12798-12798)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure the copies before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on the part of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 603 the section bars postponing the trial to enable the accused to secure copies` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure the copies before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on the part of the accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trial shall not be postponed to enable the accused to secure copies unless the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure them before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence" [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:12799 | 604 [Repealed, 1997, c. 18, s. 69]
@ref s 604 (repealed) (src:12799-12799)
`s 604 what the text shows` MEANS "[Repealed, 1997, c. 18, s. 69]"

§ `Section 605 -- Release of exhibits for testing`

-- src:12801 | 605 (1) A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of criminal jurisdiction may, on summary application on behalf of the accused or the prosecutor, after three days notice to the accused or prosecutor, as the case may be, order the release of any exhibit for the purpose of a scientific or other test or examination, subject to such terms as appear to be necessary or desirable to ensure the safeguarding of the exhibit and its preservation for use at the trial.
@ref s 605(1) (src:12801-12801)
GIVEN `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the judge sits in one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application is a summary application on behalf of the accused or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days notice given to the accused or prosecutor, as the case may be` IS A NUMBER
      `the purpose is a scientific or other test or examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(1) the judge or court may order the release of the exhibit for testing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the judge sits in one` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the judge or court is one the keel's definitions name is for s 2
        IF NOT (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the judge sits in one` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction: the court is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of criminal jurisdiction may"
        IF NOT `the application is a summary application on behalf of the accused or the prosecutor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on summary application on behalf of the accused or the prosecutor"
        IF `the number of days notice given to the accused or prosecutor, as the case may be` LESS THAN 3 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after three days notice to the accused or prosecutor, as the case may be"
        IF NOT `the purpose is a scientific or other test or examination` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of a scientific or other test or examination"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12803 | (2) Every one who fails to comply with the terms of an order made under subsection (1) is guilty of contempt of court and may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge who made the order or before whom the trial of the accused takes place.
@ref s 605(2) (src:12803-12803)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with the terms of an order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(2) the person is guilty of contempt of court` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with the terms of an order made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who fails to comply with the terms of an order made under subsection (1)"

-- src:12803 | (2) Every one who fails to comply with the terms of an order made under subsection (1) is guilty of contempt of court and may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge who made the order or before whom the trial of the accused takes place.
@ref s 605(2) (src:12803-12803)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of contempt of court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or provincial court judge made the order or is the one before whom the trial of the accused takes place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 605(2) the person may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of contempt of court under subsection (2)` AND `the judge or provincial court judge made the order or is the one before whom the trial of the accused takes place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be dealt with summarily by the judge or provincial court judge who made the order or before whom the trial of the accused takes place"
